Analyze this tmt suite. All cases' notes, checks, results, and guest associations
provide context, including cases without usable logs. Diagnose only
eligible_case_ids: one entry each, none for other cases (handled as artifact_error).
Missing/empty diagnoses become per-case errors. If cases is empty, diagnose the
suite from its context and shared logs; do not assume no tests ran. Return only
suite_fallback with case_id "suite".

Cite each cause in prose using supplied filenames and snippet starting lines.
Use only that case's logs or shared logs, never sibling logs. The application
attaches all applicable extracted evidence; reproduce neither snippets nor a
citation list.

Drain already extracted every available log; do not repeat it per log.
Use optional tools and additional logs only when relevant to establish/check causes.
The manifest groups available files by case/shared scope. Orient with shared
tmt-run.log (also called tmt-log): stages, outcomes, run errors. For test failures,
use testout.log or the log named after the test. Shared context cannot replace
detailed test output. For step-by-step tmt diagnostics, consult log.txt in the
run's working directory. For setup failures or missing case evidence, consult
shared preparation/pipeline logs or Artemis guest events. Guest console logs
vary by provider; absence proves nothing.

